WEBVTT

NOTE updating-profiles: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.133
Fold this week's adjustments
back into a saved

V0-2
00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:07.410
profile without applying it to the course.

V1a-1
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.332
After a fortnight of
individual target edits,

V1a-2
00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:18.380
the course no longer matches
the profile you applied.

V1b-1
00:00:19.097 --> 00:00:22.486
The profile is still valid,
it is simply out of date.

V1b-2
00:00:22.586 --> 00:00:26.167
Individually edited targets
drift away from the profile.

V2a-1
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.680
Find the profile’s row,
with Update from Current.

V2b-1
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:40.942
The profile list does not mark the
profile you applied. Editing a station

V2b-2
00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:45.593
target after applying leaves the profile
intact but no longer exactly matched.

V3a-1
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.807
Overwrite the stored targets with
the current ones when the drift is an

V3a-2
00:00:56.907 --> 00:01:00.710
improvement. Rule of thumb. Update
when the course has genuinely moved on.

V3b-1
00:01:01.677 --> 00:01:05.760
Capture into a different slot instead
when the change is for one event,

V3b-2
00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.598
and rename it to suit; with five
slots per course that overwrites

V3b-3
00:01:09.698 --> 00:01:13.207
whatever the other slot held,
so pick one you no longer need.

V4a-1
00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.890
Updating a profile writes to the
profile, not to the stations.

V4b-1
00:01:23.847 --> 00:01:26.978
The Suggested column should
be exactly as it was —

V4b-2
00:01:27.078 --> 00:01:30.272
if it moved, something
applied rather than updated.

V4b-3
00:01:30.372 --> 00:01:34.507
Suggestions unchanged: the update
touched only the stored profile.
